<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36226" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">physis</span></b> , is,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>nature.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: seu cupis genitor vocari et auctor
			orbis aut physis ipsa Panque, Poët. in Anth. Lat. t. 2, p.
			474 Burm.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic., <i>partycolored precious stones which had
				no distinctive name</i>, <i>freaks of nature</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				37, 12, 74, § 195</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
